Check:
Static: no entrypoint, hook command or CI step calls `vibe`, except the audit job of C-04 and `vibe --version` in a CI job that calls no entrypoint. Execution: with `vibe` not on `PATH`, `verify` passes in the probe copy and the A-02 deny cases are still refused.

Part check (static):
no entrypoint, hook command or CI step calls `vibe`, except the audit job of C-04 and `vibe --version` in a CI job that calls no entrypoint.

Part check (execution):
with `vibe` not on `PATH`, `verify` passes in the probe copy and the A-02 deny cases are still refused.

Details:
Calls of vibe:
  Under contract 2.x, a command calls `vibe` when the last path element of
  its first word, after `/` or `\`, is the literal `vibe` or `vibe.exe`,
  compared case-sensitively. The directory part may hold an expansion, so
  `"$dir/vibe" verify` and `./bin/vibe verify` are calls. A last element
  that holds an expansion, such as `"$bin" verify`, is not. `vibe-guard` by
  any path is not a call of `vibe`. C-04's audit job and the `vibe --version`
  exemption recognize `vibe` the same way.
  Under contract 1.x, its first word must be the literal `vibe`.
